# Build and test output
/build/
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Compiled examples. Each example is package main in its own directory, so a
# bare `go build ./...` drops an executable beside the source, named after the
# directory it came from -- and one of them reached a commit here at eighteen
# megabytes. This repository is public and its history is fetched by Go's
# module mirror, so a binary committed once is one every clone carries.
#
# Named one by one rather than globbed. A pattern wide enough to catch an
# extensionless binary is wide enough to hide a source file nobody notices is
# missing, and in a public repository that is the worse failure.
/examples/orbit/orbit
/examples/observe/observe

# Local dependencies and workspaces
/vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum

# Local run directories for live checks. The vanilla server task writes a world,
# logs, and a jar copy here; none of it belongs in a public repository, and the
# jar is a Mojang artifact that must stay local.
/.local/

# Local configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.direnv/
.devbox/
.task/

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/

